      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "After stent implantation there is a high risk of acute stent thrombosis. Therefore, a very aggressive anticoagulation drug regimen is necessary. Two patients developed large hematomas of the upperarm that where presumably caused by automatic blood pressure measuring equipment or by a tourniquet used during blood collection. In one patient a complete paralysis of the ulnar and radial nerves resulted."},
